45
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:41,340
That's perfect.

46
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:44,300
Even 15 minutes can make a big difference.

47
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:46,740
Another mistake people make is arriving late.

48
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,820
Yes, that happened to me.

49
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:53,860
The traffic was bad and I walked in feeling stressed and flustered.

50
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:56,500
Arriving late creates a negative first impression.

51
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,420
Try to plan to arrive early.

52
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:02,840
10-15 minutes before the interview gives you time to relax.

53
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:09,180
Next time I'll aim to arrive at least 20 minutes early, even if it means leaving home earlier.

54
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:10,180
Great plan.

55
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:15,940
And if something unexpected happens, a polite apology and a smile show professionalism.

56
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:18,300
Another problem I had was body language.

57
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:23,380
I was so nervous that I kept fidgeting with my hands and looking down.

58
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:25,660
Body language is very important.

59
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:32,220
Your posture, avoiding eye contact, or fidgeting can make you seem insecure or uninterested.

60
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:37,340
I didn't realize crossing my arms or looking away could send the wrong message.

61
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:38,340
Yes.

62
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:43,220
Sit straight, relax your hands, make natural eye contact, and smile a little.

63
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,380
You can practice in front of a mirror at home.

64
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:46,980
That's a good idea.

65
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:50,460
I also made a mistake when talking about my previous job.

66
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:53,460
