74
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:16,280
Another common mistake is not asking questions at the end.

75
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:17,280
Yes.

76
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:20,280
I said no, because I couldn't think of anything.

77
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:23,280
Asking questions shows interest and curiosity.

78
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:28,040
There are two to three questions in advance, like, what does a typical day look like?

79
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:31,200
Or what skills are important to succeed here?

80
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,200
That's smart.

81
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:35,840
Even simple questions are good as long as they show motivation.

82
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:40,280
Yes, and remember to slow down your speech if you get nervous.

83
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,560
Silence is okay.

84
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:44,000
You can pause and think before answering.

85
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,840
I always felt I had to answer immediately.

86
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:50,920
Now I see that pausing can actually make me look more confident.

87
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:51,920
Exactly.

88
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:54,040
You can say, that's a good question.

89
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,360
Let me think for a moment.

90
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:57,360
It's natural and professional.

91
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:59,880
I feel much calmer already.

92
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:03,760
Remember, interviews are conversations, not exams.

93
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:08,520
You don't need perfect English, just clear ideas and a positive attitude.

94
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,640
That really helps.

95
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:14,000
I used to worry about my accent or small grammar mistakes.

96
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,040
Don't worry about your accent.

97
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:21,300
Interviewers focus more on your skills, attitude, and communication than perfection.

98
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,300
Thank you, Jessica.

99
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:25,940
I feel more confident and motivated to prepare better.

100
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:27,300
